[[2047,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>ABS electronic control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nsupplied (at pins 12 and 6) directly by the battery via a line protected\nby the ABS maxifuse, located directly on the battery \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               -\nconnector C.</p><p>The supply controlled by the ignition (15/54)\nreaches pin 23 from the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F6</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the\nadditional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit is earthed via pins 1 and\n5.</p><p>The four sensors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K70, K71, K75, K76</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              send\nwheel speed signals to pins 12-28, 16-15, 14-13 and 30-31 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               respectively.</p><p>Brake pedal switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends a &#x27;pedal\ndepressed&#x27; enablement signal to pin 32 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\nthe ABS cannot intervene unless the brake pedal is pressed.</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a &#x27;pedal\nreleased&#x27; signal, double switch, at pin 20.</p><p>The &#x27;ASR OFF&#x27; control button on panel \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H35</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends\na deactivation signal to pin 28 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while pin 27 relays\na signal that turns on an LED on panel \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H35</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               when the system\nis off.</p><p>Steering sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K58</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied by\nABS control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               at pin 39 and receives a reference earth\nfrom pin 21: the signal that detects sudden changes in steering\ndirection is sent via the CAN line to engine control unit  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and ABS\ncontrol unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pins 24 and 40).</p><p>The CAN line that connects \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (from\npins 24 and 40) to \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               allows the ASR function to notify\nthe engine management control unit of excessive engine power.  this\nline is not direct, but passes through the steering sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K58</strong><a href=\"#/3234515\">E5030</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234559\">E5050</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Yaw sensor  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K74</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied from\nABS control unit  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               at pin 39, while it receives a reference\nearth from pin 21: control and command signals are exchanged with\nABS control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , at pins 8, 9, 10 and 41.</p><p>Pressure sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K72</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied from\nABS control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               at pin 42, while it receives a reference\nearth from pin 25: the pressure detection signal is sent to pin\n26 of  ABS control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>If the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              detects problems\nrelating to the ABS function, it sends the speedometer instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               a\nsignal from pin 22, which lights up the &#x27;ABS failure&#x27; warning light;\nthe lighting up of the &#x27;VDC&#x27; warning light is also managed via the\nsame line; If the problems concern the EBD function, the handbrake\nwarning light is lit up from pin 38 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .; these are earth\nsignals, and they cause the warning lights to come on, becuase the\ninstrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               supply is controlled by the ignition (INT)\nfrom the line protected by fuse F4 of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 37 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               produces a speedometer\nsignal (average speed of all four wheels) which is sent to the instrument\n panel \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong><a href=\"#/3234310\">E4021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The autodiagnostic data can be read by connecting\nto connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : it receives signals from pin 11 of the\ncontrol unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via the special diagnostic line.</p>"]]